# public/_headers  (copied verbatim into the build output)
#
# Security baseline plus cache policy. Works the same on Workers Assets and on
# Pages. See CLOUDFLARE.md, "stack-independent contracts".
#
# THE RULE THAT SURPRISES PEOPLE: these rules are ADDITIVE, not override.
# A more specific path does NOT beat a broader one. Every rule whose pattern
# matches contributes its headers, and a header set by two matching rules is
# joined with a comma. Layering a narrow rule on top of a broad one that sets
# the same header produces something like:
#
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# which is malformed, and the FIRST max-age wins regardless of which rule was
# more specific. Write one flat rule per prefix instead.
#
# Also note: none of this applies to responses generated by Worker code,
# including when run_worker_first is set. Set those headers in the script.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Deliberately no Cache-Control above. Adding one there would concatenate with
# every more specific rule below, for every asset those rules match.

# Content-hashed build output. A content change produces a new filename, so
# these are safe to freeze forever. Adjust the prefix to your bundler:
# /_astro/* for Astro, /assets/* for a default Vite build.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Hand-authored files that keep their name across deploys can NEVER be
# immutable, or an edit never reaches anyone who has already visited. An hour
# of freshness with a day of stale-while-revalidate keeps repeat navigations
# off the origin without stranding a deploy.
# /static-page/*
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Data the site rewrites on a schedule must revalidate. Do not fold this into
# a broader immutable rule.
# /data/*
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
